{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778944125,"nonce":"syzUFJ1O7B0lkm8SUC8JTucK2AI=","message":"## Updated navigation direction: left app rail, not top button strip\n\nMLL clarified a newer product direction during the ledger planning work: Mandible's top-level navigation should move away from a row of buttons in the title/top bar and toward a leftmost application sidebar/rail, closer to VS Code or similar desktop apps.\n\nUpdated design direction:\n\n- leftmost rail is the top-level navigation across Mandible views;\n- the rail can eventually collapse to icons only, with labels/tooltips as needed;\n- each view may still have its own secondary sidebar immediately to the right of the rail;\n- the secondary sidebar is view-specific, e.g. conversation list for unified Chat, issue list for Issues, graph filters/layers for Graph, auth queue filters/history for Auth;\n- the previous idea of merely rearranging top header buttons should be considered superseded unless a narrow interim patch is needed.\n\nThis also aligns with the new unified Chat/History issue 10a4214: the Chat workspace should have an app-rail entry plus a conversation sidebar, not a top tab plus sub-tabs for live sessions.\n\nImplementation should treat this as an application shell/layout refactor, not a cosmetic tab reorder. It needs keyboard navigation, deep-link preservation, responsive/collapsed behavior, and no top-level page scroll/wiggle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}